## Audit log

`modules/audit/` keeps an append-only record of who did what. In a service,
inside the unit of work it describes:

```python
from {{ name.package }}.modules.audit.public import record_audit_event

await record_audit_event(
    self.session,
    action="transfer.approved",
    actor_id=user.id,
    target_type="transfer",
    target_id=str(transfer.id),
    details={"amount": str(transfer.amount)},
)
await self.session.commit()
```

It never commits on its own, so the entry is kept with the change or rolled
back with it. The repository refuses to change or delete entries. With auth,
every sign-in, failure, lock and token reuse is recorded as `auth.<event>`.
